You are 100% correct, and I completely agree with your architectural assessment.
Calling it csvDate in the backend was a legacy naming convention left over from when the system only processed CSVs. Since it conceptually represents the POSTING_DATE in the database for both Excel and CSV files, **we should standardize the name to postingDate across the entire stack (Frontend -> Backend DTO -> Database).**
Instead of forcing your React frontend to use the old csvDate name, we will fix the Spring Boot backend to accept postingDate.
Here are the exact changes you need to make to fully standardize this.
