### Summary of Why This is Better
By making these changes in the Java backend, you achieve complete **Domain Language Consistency**.
 * The User Interface says "Posting Date"
 * The React state is postingDate
 * The JSON Payload is {"postingDate": "2026-02-28"}
 * The Java DTO is postingDate
 * The Database is POSTING_DATE
This eliminates confusion permanently and prevents the exact mapping mismatch that caused your 500 error earlier. Excellent catch on realizing the naming was logically flawed!
